  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Given \\(a+b=5\\) and \\(a-b=2\\), find the value of \\(a^2-b^2\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "10",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(a^2-b^2=(a+b)(a-b)=5\\times2=10\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Find a and b by elimination\n\nThe given sum and difference let us find \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) by eliminating one variable. Adding the equations gives \\(2a=7\\), so \\(a=\\frac{7}{2}\\). Subtracting the second equation from the first gives \\(2b=3\\), so \\(b=\\frac{3}{2}\\). Therefore\n\\[\na^2-b^2=\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{49-9}{4}=10.\n\\]",
